You type a prompt → a multi-agent AI system generates a playable HTML5 game (art, audio, mechanics, code).
The game is published into a vertical, TikTok-style feed of instant-play, portrait, browser games — no download, no install.
Other users play, rate, remix, and follow.

AI (creation cost → ~0)
   > CREATORS (anyone, no code)
      > GAMES (supply: 75k+, growing daily)
         > FEED / ALGORITHM (zero-friction distribution)
            > PLAYS & ATTENTION (140M plays/mo)
               > MONETIZATION (ads / IAP / brands)
                  > CREATOR PAYOUTS ($10M fund)
                     ↺ back to CREATORS (more, and better ones)

NEW GAMES (appear constant, increase desire to return) > FEED+ALGORITHM (zero-friction distribution) > AUDIENCE > ADS + IN-GAME PURCHASES + BRAND GAMES > REVENUE SHARE (platform keeps a take rate, creators keep the rest)

The platform becomes a fusion of TOOL (generate a game) and DISTIBUTION CHANNEL (discovery + monetization)

Revenue:
Rewarded video + interstitial ads  
In-game purchases / platform currency with a take rate
Native ads (branded games)

----------

Risks slide:
Quality floor	AI makes it easy to make a game, not a good game. 
Unit economics  GPU inference costs. If ad ARPU per play lands below inference cost per play, the model fails arithmetic.
